  <div class="site-content">
    <div class="verification-strip"><span class="verification-long">Lean gate passed before this site build; local proof declarations are shown as compiled.</span><span class="verification-short">Lean-verified build · exact declarations linked.</span></div>
    <div class="page-shell">
      <main class="page-main" id="main-content"><nav class="book-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="../index.html">Books</a><span aria-hidden="true"> / </span><span aria-current="page">Online Learning Book</span></nav><section class="hero" id="book"><p class="eyebrow">Source-mapped reading view</p><h1 class="page-title">Online Learning Book</h1><p class="lede">Orabona v10 shares one canonical Lean library: Chapter 1 foundations, extended convexity, closure constructions and supporting gradients, projected OGD with fixed or decreasing steps, and subsequent bounded Chapter 2 packages. Probability, EXP3 and Tsallis references remain shared. Chapter 2 and the Chapters 1-16 program remain incomplete.</p><article class="book-source"><h2>Online Learning: A Modern Introduction Using Convex Optimization</h2>
<p>Francesco Orabona</p><p>arXiv:1912.13213v10, June 21, 2026; final preprint</p>
<p><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1912.13213v10">Read the source ↗</a> · <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1912.13213">Official source page ↗</a></p>
<small>Bibliographic metadata checked 2026-09-13. Page and theorem mappings are separately audited.</small></article></section><section id="existing-reading"><h2>Existing shared reading</h2><p>Source-scoped packages are identified on their chapter pages. Their exact completion boundaries do not cover the rest of this book; older shared reading links retain their original sources.</p><ol class="shared-route"><li><a href="../../chapters/online-foundations/index.html">Online Learning: foundations and Follow-the-Leader</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-convex/index.html">Convexity with extended-real values</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-convex-closures/index.html">Convexity-preserving constructions</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-first-order/index.html">Supporting gradients for extended-real losses</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-optimality/index.html">Constrained convex optimality</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-expectation/index.html">Signed expectation foundations for Jensen</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-barycenter/index.html">Means in arbitrary finite-dimensional convex sets</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-minorant/index.html">Affine lower bounds on arbitrary convex domains</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-jensen/index.html">Jensen with possibly infinite expected loss</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-ftl-failure/index.html">Why Follow-the-Leader can incur linear regret</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-guessing-ogd/index.html">Projected OGD for the squared-loss guessing game</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-huber/index.html">Huber linear prediction with unconstrained OGD</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-closed-proper/index.html">Closed and proper extended-real functions</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-subgradient-basic/index.html">Global subgradients and convex restrictions</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-subgradient-interior/index.html">Global subgradients at relative interior points</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-subgradient-differentiability/index.html">A singleton global support produces the derivative</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-subgradient-sum/index.html">Subgradients of finite sums</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-subgradient-absolute/index.html">Absolute-value subdifferential</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-normal-cone/index.html">Indicator supports and normal cones</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-subgradient-max/index.html">Subdifferential of a finite maximum</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-hinge/index.html">Hinge-loss subdifferential</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-affine-subgradient/index.html">Affine transport of subgradients</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-lipschitz/index.html">Lipschitz bounds and uncountable nonsmoothness</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-osd/index.html">Causal projected online subgradient descent</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-guessing-osd/index.html">Absolute-loss guessing by projected subgradient descent</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-osd-policy/index.html">Projected OSD with legal history-dependent support policies</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-linearization/index.html">Convex losses to causal linear feedback</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-ogd/index.html">Projected OGD: Orabona Chapter 2</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-optimal-step/index.html">Optimal step size for a frozen scalar bound</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/online-unit-scaling/index.html">Units and actual OSD coordinate transport</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/probability/index.html">2. Probability, kernels, filtrations, and concentration</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/exp3/index.html">7. EXP3 and adversarial concentration</a></li><li><a href="../../chapters/tsallis/index.html">8. Tsallis-FTRL, corruption, and nonstationarity</a></li></ol></section>
<section id="planned-mapping"><h2>Remaining source mapping</h2><p>The mapped routes have bounded source contracts and exact Lean references. Remaining chapters and results require separate source and proof audits; neither this chapter nor the whole book is complete.</p></section><section id="shared-graph"><h2>One underlying Lean graph</h2><p>All references resolve to canonical declarations in the global index. Reading views do not create additional Lean modules.</p><p><a href="../../lean-graph/index.html">Explore the graph</a> · <a href="../registry.json">Download the shared reference registry</a></p></section></main>
